{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794426060,"nonce":"vMu5YPRWQ3HPzbKAF8npm+Hlczg=","title":"A shut collapsible, accordion section or tree group does not open again","message":"Open and shut a section, then open it again: the chevron turns but the content stays at no height. The first open works. Seen on the components site (accordion, tree) in headless Chrome driven by chromedriver.\n\nCause: the runners (web, desktop rebuild stage, iOS) call apply_stylesheet_layout_overrides after every update that needs layout. The pass matches rules against the registry's classes, which include signal-bound ones such as data-state=closed, and folded every match into the node's base snapshot. The snapshot then held `height: 0`, and dropping the class refolded to it. Headless does not call the pass after property updates, so no recorder test saw it.\n\nFix: the pass matches rules with the classes a node holds as a layer withheld, so only the node's own rules reach the snapshot. Tests: blinc_layout class_when (a_layout_pass_*) and the cn accordion, collapsible and tree in-place scenes, whose frame step now applies the pass as a runner does.\n\nOpen:\n- Headless could apply the pass as the runners do. Doing so moves the cn_time_picker_24_dark golden (372 px, largest channel difference 52); find which of the two is right before changing it.\n- The components page shows the shadow shader warning \"code is unreachable\" in Chrome, from the return kept after discard (see the Windows FXC issue).","files":null}]}